1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:00,873
(All characters, locations,
and events are fictional

2
00:00:00,898 --> 00:00:01,801
and for entertainment
purposes only.

3
00:00:01,826 --> 00:00:02,785
No actions depicted are intended
to be encouraged or endorsed.

4
00:00:02,810 --> 00:00:03,928
Animals were specially trained
and supervised by professionals.

5
00:00:03,952 --> 00:00:05,000
Viewer discretion is advised.)

6
00:00:12,902 --> 00:00:15,578
The difference
between winners and losers

7
00:00:15,603 --> 00:00:18,364
isn't who can hit
the ball farther,

8
00:00:18,389 --> 00:00:22,590
but who can stay focused
and steady on the crucial shots.

9
00:00:24,491 --> 00:00:27,225
Golf isn't a game of perfection.

10
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:30,371
It's a game of accepting
our mistakes.

11
00:00:30,396 --> 00:00:33,462
We may practice our swings
hundreds of times,

12
00:00:33,969 --> 00:00:36,433
but the moment the clubface
hits the ball,

13
00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:39,316
all that matters is keeping calm.

14
00:00:42,567 --> 00:00:44,386
And no matter what happens,

15
00:00:44,411 --> 00:00:47,111
we have to keep
moving on to the next hole

16
00:00:47,136 --> 00:00:48,627
until the game is over.

17
00:00:51,973 --> 00:00:58,240
(Pro Praew
Pattharaporn Sriphatprasit)

18
00:01:04,091 --> 00:01:07,617
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

19
00:01:08,086 --> 00:01:09,980
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

20
00:01:10,005 --> 00:01:13,752
♪ It's plain to see ♪

21
00:01:13,777 --> 00:01:15,754
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

22
00:01:15,778 --> 00:01:19,279
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

23
00:01:19,583 --> 00:01:21,583
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

24
00:01:21,608 --> 00:01:25,118
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

25
00:01:25,374 --> 00:01:27,374
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

26
00:01:27,399 --> 00:01:30,268
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

27
00:01:30,293 --> 00:01:32,230
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

28
00:01:32,255 --> 00:01:35,050
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

29
00:01:35,075 --> 00:01:37,918
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

30
00:01:37,943 --> 00:01:41,780
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

31
00:01:41,805 --> 00:01:43,805
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

32
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:46,595
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

33
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:50,026
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

34
00:01:50,051 --> 00:01:54,785
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

35
00:01:54,810 --> 00:01:56,817
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

36
00:01:58,654 --> 00:02:00,544
Ms. Fahsai told me

37
00:02:00,569 --> 00:02:02,912
that everything
you've done for me

38
00:02:02,937 --> 00:02:04,771
was just to charm me

39
00:02:04,796 --> 00:02:06,599
because you wanted to use me.

40
00:02:06,624 --> 00:02:09,185
But I don't believe that.

41
00:02:09,210 --> 00:02:11,793
I just want to hear you say
that's not true.

42
00:02:11,818 --> 00:02:13,818
I would never do that to you.

43
00:02:14,271 --> 00:02:16,940
You know
how real what we have is.

44
00:02:16,965 --> 00:02:18,785
And I think that's a good thing.

45
00:02:18,810 --> 00:02:21,572
It's a chance for me to reconnect
with my feelings.

46
00:02:22,399 --> 00:02:24,552
The only player
who can truly match Pro Jin

47
00:02:24,577 --> 00:02:26,831
is probably Pro Vee
from Goodview.

48
00:02:26,856 --> 00:02:28,771
Win the All Star championship.

49
00:02:28,796 --> 00:02:30,392
By any means necessary.

50
00:02:30,417 --> 00:02:33,424
Of course.
We have to win this match.

51
00:03:10,830 --> 00:03:13,565
"I saw you were still asleep,
so I left first.

52
00:03:13,590 --> 00:03:15,590
See you at the course, Your Vee."

53
00:03:36,509 --> 00:03:37,818
- Hello.
- Hi.

54
00:03:46,398 --> 00:03:47,731
Ugh, where did Nana go?

55
00:03:48,137 --> 00:03:49,615
I haven't seen her
since I got here.

56
00:03:53,530 --> 00:03:57,108
Nut, something's happened.

57
00:03:57,364 --> 00:04:00,783
The announcer we hired
isn't answering any of our calls.

58
00:04:00,808 --> 00:04:03,345
And the event starts
in ten minutes.

59
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:05,554
- Oh.
- Does Nana know?

60
00:04:05,797 --> 00:04:08,175
I haven't seen Miss Nana
since this morning.

61
00:04:18,181 --> 00:04:19,785
There she is.

62
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:23,420
Whoa, where have you been?

63
00:04:25,649 --> 00:04:28,674
- Miss Nana, there's something...
- I already know.

64
00:04:28,748 --> 00:04:31,454
It's nothing major.
Every problem has a solution.

65
00:04:37,842 --> 00:04:41,472
Hello!
Welcome to Goodview Golf Club.

66
00:04:43,710 --> 00:04:47,964
Oh, thank you, March,
for the shrimp soup you sent me.

67
00:04:48,767 --> 00:04:50,619
Did you come to see
who wins today,

68
00:04:50,644 --> 00:04:53,740
or to see which of your plans
falls apart next?

69
00:04:57,866 --> 00:04:59,945
And about your plan this morning,

70
00:04:59,970 --> 00:05:01,995
I don't think
it was yours, March,

71
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:05,379
Because it was... baby stuff!

72
00:05:05,897 --> 00:05:08,222
Oops, someone's calling.

73
00:05:10,216 --> 00:05:11,464
What the hell?

74
00:05:24,019 --> 00:05:25,058
Oops!

75
00:05:38,771 --> 00:05:40,171
Is that all you've got?

76
00:05:43,883 --> 00:05:44,930
Whoa!

77
00:05:48,831 --> 00:05:50,458
Guess this counts
as my morning workout.

78
00:05:54,837 --> 00:05:55,939
Nice try.

79
00:06:03,942 --> 00:06:04,960
Oh!

80
00:06:06,492 --> 00:06:07,516
Huh!

81
00:06:09,122 --> 00:06:10,233
You're still not done?

82
00:06:15,063 --> 00:06:16,646
How am I supposed
to get past this one?

83
00:06:22,254 --> 00:06:23,380
Here goes nothing.

84
00:06:34,106 --> 00:06:36,388
What movie did
whoever planned this watch?

85
00:06:36,397 --> 00:06:39,120
That's such a childish plan.

86
00:06:43,842 --> 00:06:44,897
You're pretty good.

87
00:06:56,974 --> 00:06:59,317
The event looks amazing, Nana.

88
00:07:01,551 --> 00:07:02,979
Thank you, Auntie.

89
00:07:03,474 --> 00:07:06,142
See? This is exactly
what I was telling you.

90
00:07:06,167 --> 00:07:08,621
- I could retire tomorrow.
- Mm-hmm.

91
00:07:10,223 --> 00:07:13,465
Uh, but Miss Nana,
about the announcer...

92
00:07:15,006 --> 00:07:17,281
I'll have to ask you
to fill in, Nut.

93
00:07:17,306 --> 00:07:18,973
But don't worry
about being lonely.

94
00:07:18,998 --> 00:07:20,724
I've already asked Chef Queen

95
00:07:20,749 --> 00:07:22,597
to help you
with the commentary, too.

96
00:07:22,756 --> 00:07:23,772
Oh...

97
00:07:25,525 --> 00:07:28,452
Sure. Then I'll go get ready.

98
00:07:29,319 --> 00:07:31,350
I'll leave things here to Belle.

99
00:07:31,574 --> 00:07:32,797
Of course.

100
00:07:32,979 --> 00:07:34,503
- Excuse me.
- Sure.

101
00:07:52,595 --> 00:07:56,844
Hello, everyone, and welcome to

102
00:07:56,869 --> 00:08:00,450
the All Star Women's
Golf Championship.

103
00:08:00,475 --> 00:08:02,413
Featuring the finest
female golfers

104
00:08:02,438 --> 00:08:05,016
from the country's
top golf clubs,

105
00:08:05,041 --> 00:08:08,956
all vying for a title that's more
than just a championship.

106
00:08:14,715 --> 00:08:16,807
And now, let me introduce

107
00:08:16,832 --> 00:08:20,588
the players competing in
today's tournament.

108
00:08:20,782 --> 00:08:26,036
First up, Pro Pop, Ploychompoo,
from Sky Valley Golf Club.

109
00:08:29,236 --> 00:08:35,546
And next, Pro Kaimook, Yanisa,
from The Blue Lake Golf Course.

110
00:08:39,278 --> 00:08:43,701
Pro Sherry, Tiranan,
from Legacy V Golf Club.

111
00:08:45,798 --> 00:08:51,033
And next, Pro Meiji, Jenjira,
from Golden Hill.

112
00:08:52,619 --> 00:08:57,302
Pro Satang, Kornkamol,
from Angel Golf Country Club.

113
00:08:58,458 --> 00:09:03,793
And next, Pro Wine, Nattagate,
from Royal Horizon Golf Links.

114
00:09:04,410 --> 00:09:10,552
And finally, Pro Jin, Jintaphat,
from The Royal Green.

115
00:09:11,598 --> 00:09:13,181
I don't like
leaving things to chance.

116
00:09:13,733 --> 00:09:16,838
I want to know for certain,
before you even compete,

117
00:09:16,863 --> 00:09:18,222
that you're going to win.

118
00:09:18,247 --> 00:09:21,541
This is a ball drop device.
Just strap it to your ankle.

119
00:09:21,566 --> 00:09:24,022
And this is a rangefinder
I modified myself.

120
00:09:24,047 --> 00:09:26,047
You can use its slope mode.

121
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:28,645
Don't forget to wear
long pants tomorrow.

122
00:09:29,094 --> 00:09:30,629
So you can hide the device.

123
00:09:47,450 --> 00:09:49,263
Don't worry, Ms. Yupadee.

124
00:09:49,288 --> 00:09:51,548
Pro Jin won't use the ball drop
device. But we still...

125
00:09:51,573 --> 00:09:53,414
Pro Jin told me
to return it to you, Mr. March.

126
00:09:55,723 --> 00:09:56,730
Why?

127
00:09:57,657 --> 00:10:00,020
She said she'll use
her own rangefinder.

128
00:10:00,045 --> 00:10:02,300
She tried this one,
but couldn't see through it.

129
00:10:02,325 --> 00:10:03,625
Couldn't see through it?

130
00:10:05,293 --> 00:10:06,416
Looks fine to me.

131
00:10:07,329 --> 00:10:10,200
Pro Jin said she couldn't see
the future with it.

132
00:10:10,225 --> 00:10:11,494
And when she adjusted
the slope mode,

133
00:10:11,519 --> 00:10:13,177
it made a suspicious sound.

134
00:10:13,201 --> 00:10:14,973
So she told me to return it.

135
00:10:19,376 --> 00:10:21,179
Pro Jin's pretty crafty,
isn't she?

136
00:10:21,973 --> 00:10:24,777
And your plan isn't scary at all.

137
00:10:25,329 --> 00:10:27,321
It's actually pretty funny now.

138
00:10:28,068 --> 00:10:29,490
What other plans do you have?

139
00:10:30,535 --> 00:10:31,725
Of course I have more.

140
00:10:32,835 --> 00:10:33,897
Just wait and see.

141
00:10:46,555 --> 00:10:49,488
And finally, representing
our very own course,

142
00:10:49,513 --> 00:10:54,037
Pro Venus
from Goodview Golf Club!

143
00:10:54,708 --> 00:10:58,251
(Pro Venus - Goodview Golf Club)

144
00:11:01,882 --> 00:11:04,971
- Pro Vee! Pro Vee...
- Pro Vee! Pro Vee...

145
00:11:06,081 --> 00:11:08,817
(Pro Venus - Goodview Golf Club)

146
00:11:17,551 --> 00:11:20,013
(Pro Venus - Goodview Golf Club)

147
00:11:27,930 --> 00:11:33,100
I hope you won't pull any more
dirty tricks like you did before.

148
00:11:34,710 --> 00:11:38,381
I assure you,
I won't do anything like that.

149
00:11:38,789 --> 00:11:41,725
Wow, and here's
the official opening shot

150
00:11:41,750 --> 00:11:43,750
to kick off the tournament!

151
00:11:44,098 --> 00:11:46,845
Today's competition
will be divided into two groups.

152
00:11:46,870 --> 00:11:49,855
Group A has four players,
and Group B has four.

153
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:52,716
Group A will start on Hole 1,

154
00:11:52,741 --> 00:11:55,465
while Group B
will start on Hole 10.

155
00:11:55,664 --> 00:11:57,816
They'll play through
all 18 holes.

156
00:11:57,841 --> 00:12:01,462
But Nat, why don't we all start
on Hole 1 together?

157
00:12:01,570 --> 00:12:04,538
It's simple.
With a two-tee start,

158
00:12:04,563 --> 00:12:08,065
both groups can finish almost
at the same time.

159
00:12:08,150 --> 00:12:10,436
Since they can
start playing simultaneously,

160
00:12:10,461 --> 00:12:13,024
neither group has to wait for
the other to start.

161
00:12:13,049 --> 00:12:14,726
Then the other group
follows behind.

162
00:12:14,751 --> 00:12:18,100
Oh, I see. So the scoreboard will
show everyone's current score,

163
00:12:18,125 --> 00:12:19,863
so we can see who's leading.

164
00:12:19,888 --> 00:12:22,451
And we'll get to see the winner
right in front of us, right?

165
00:12:22,476 --> 00:12:23,949
- Exactly.
- Wow!

166
00:12:23,974 --> 00:12:26,733
Let's take a look at
the opening shots.

167
00:12:32,225 --> 00:12:35,759
(Pro Venus)

168
00:12:42,688 --> 00:12:45,912
Wow, what a beautiful
opening shot, Pro Venus!

169
00:14:11,701 --> 00:14:13,655
That was an incredible shot!

170
00:14:23,403 --> 00:14:25,582
Pro Jin is going aggressive
with this shot,

171
00:14:25,607 --> 00:14:26,847
taking a bold risk.

172
00:14:26,872 --> 00:14:30,308
The players are all very close
on the leaderboard right now.

173
00:14:45,886 --> 00:14:49,129
If this ball reaches the green,
she'll have a shot at eagle.

174
00:14:53,456 --> 00:14:56,623
Wow, what a beautiful
opening shot, Pro Venus!

175
00:14:57,727 --> 00:14:58,956
That's tough.

176
00:15:00,759 --> 00:15:02,017
Oh, wow!

177
00:15:29,827 --> 00:15:31,487
Beautifully done!

178
00:15:31,512 --> 00:15:34,369
That shot puts
Pro Jin in the lead.

179
00:15:50,603 --> 00:15:52,961
- Wow, great shot!
- What a shot!

180
00:15:58,647 --> 00:15:59,835
It's incredibly close.

181
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:01,756
Yes, Nut. It's really heating up.

182
00:16:01,781 --> 00:16:04,613
No one's giving
an inch right now.

183
00:16:22,799 --> 00:16:24,996
- Wow!
- Whoa!

184
00:16:25,021 --> 00:16:27,021
- What happened?
- Pro Vee missed that shot.

185
00:16:27,046 --> 00:16:28,608
What a shame.

186
00:16:31,913 --> 00:16:33,784
Now there are
only four holes left.

187
00:16:33,809 --> 00:16:36,848
We'll have to see if Pro Vee
can make up the gap

188
00:16:36,873 --> 00:16:38,786
and catch the leader, Pro Jin.
- Yes.

189
00:16:38,810 --> 00:16:41,068
Shall we recap the scores so far?

190
00:16:41,093 --> 00:16:42,554
Of course, Nat.

191
00:16:42,579 --> 00:16:46,571
Currently in first place
is Pro Jin from Group B,

192
00:16:46,596 --> 00:16:48,840
representing The Royal Green.

193
00:16:48,865 --> 00:16:53,134
In second place is Pro Kaimook,
also from Group B,

194
00:16:53,174 --> 00:16:55,960
representing Woodview Golf Club.

195
00:16:55,985 --> 00:16:57,814
Followed by Pro Wine,

196
00:16:57,839 --> 00:17:00,568
from Thai Silver Country Club.

197
00:17:00,593 --> 00:17:05,315
And in fourth place is Pro Vee
from Goodview Golf Club.

198
00:17:05,340 --> 00:17:08,035
But it's still too early to call.

199
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:10,863
In golf, anything can happen.

200
00:17:10,888 --> 00:17:12,850
We have to wait until Hole 18

201
00:17:12,875 --> 00:17:16,273
before we know who's truly
the best today.

202
00:17:16,298 --> 00:17:18,483
Oh, this is getting intense,
everyone!

203
00:17:42,410 --> 00:17:44,049
Don't get too confident yet.

204
00:17:44,350 --> 00:17:46,779
Pro Vee is closing the gap.

205
00:17:48,039 --> 00:17:49,254
Don't worry.

206
00:17:49,785 --> 00:17:51,103
She'll never catch up.

207
00:17:54,171 --> 00:17:56,404
Has anyone ever told you

208
00:17:56,429 --> 00:17:59,436
your greatest strength
is knowing how to talk?

209
00:17:59,864 --> 00:18:02,386
But your weakness is that
talk is all you do.

210
00:18:03,362 --> 00:18:05,420
Hurry up and make me believe

211
00:18:05,445 --> 00:18:08,790
our course will win
before we reach Hole 18.

212
00:18:10,942 --> 00:18:12,022
Yes, ma'am.

213
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:55,545
Here's the situation.
Pro Vee has a chance at eagle,

214
00:18:55,570 --> 00:18:58,381
while Pro Jin needs to save par.

215
00:19:14,046 --> 00:19:16,074
Do you have a plan
to close this out?

216
00:19:16,582 --> 00:19:17,719
Of course.

217
00:19:31,037 --> 00:19:32,203
Pick up, damn it!

218
00:19:34,025 --> 00:19:35,175
Why aren't you answering?

219
00:19:36,666 --> 00:19:37,782
Pick up!

220
00:19:52,146 --> 00:19:54,314
Oh, no! Who's dead now?

221
00:19:54,339 --> 00:19:55,831
There's an ambulance here now,

222
00:19:55,856 --> 00:19:58,078
and it's really distracting
the players.

223
00:19:58,103 --> 00:20:00,995
Officials, could you please check
what's happening?

224
00:20:15,654 --> 00:20:17,069
This is your plan?

225
00:20:19,236 --> 00:20:21,548
Well? What do you
think of my plan?

226
00:20:21,871 --> 00:20:24,320
It's obviously
the plan of a pathetic crook.

227
00:20:40,691 --> 00:20:42,668
It's not as close as
it should be.

228
00:20:42,693 --> 00:20:45,869
I think the next shot
will be quite a pressure shot.

229
00:20:45,894 --> 00:20:49,929
Oh, this is so nerve-racking!
I can hardly breathe!

230
00:20:49,954 --> 00:20:51,722
Let's see how this plays out.

231
00:20:55,126 --> 00:20:59,413
And now we've finally reached the
decisive hole.

232
00:20:59,438 --> 00:21:03,064
This is so exciting!
We've made it to the 18th hole.

233
00:21:03,089 --> 00:21:05,674
It looks like several players
still have a chance, right?

234
00:21:05,699 --> 00:21:08,741
Absolutely.
The final hole is a par 5.

235
00:21:08,766 --> 00:21:11,369
- Pro Jin is leading at -13.
- Yes.

236
00:21:11,394 --> 00:21:14,509
Pro Vee is just
one stroke behind at -12,

237
00:21:14,533 --> 00:21:17,378
while Pro Pop is only
two strokes behind.

238
00:21:17,403 --> 00:21:19,881
Oh, my! What could happen
with scores like these?

239
00:21:20,210 --> 00:21:22,767
If Pro Jin makes par
on this hole,

240
00:21:22,792 --> 00:21:24,204
she'll win
the championship outright.

241
00:21:24,229 --> 00:21:25,277
Oh, my God!

242
00:21:25,301 --> 00:21:28,366
As for Pro Vee,
she needs at least a birdie

243
00:21:28,391 --> 00:21:30,509
to have a chance. Just a chance.

244
00:21:30,797 --> 00:21:33,872
But to take the lead
and beat Pro Jin outright,

245
00:21:33,897 --> 00:21:36,129
she needs nothing
less than an eagle.

246
00:21:36,154 --> 00:21:39,892
Oh, my God! Everyone,
let's see how this plays out!

247
00:21:55,193 --> 00:21:58,422
Pro Jin remains calm,
sticking to her game plan.

248
00:22:17,249 --> 00:22:21,080
Oh, no! It's not going in!

249
00:22:21,105 --> 00:22:24,162
It's not going in! Not this time!

250
00:22:28,936 --> 00:22:30,974
Pro Jin just missed it.

251
00:22:30,999 --> 00:22:33,658
That puts Pro Jin at -12,

252
00:22:33,683 --> 00:22:35,049
putting her behind.

253
00:22:35,074 --> 00:22:36,994
Pro Vee now has a chance
to take the lead.

254
00:22:50,091 --> 00:22:52,019
That's why I wanted you
to compete again, Vee.

255
00:22:52,044 --> 00:22:53,886
Don't let your whole life

256
00:22:53,910 --> 00:22:56,467
end at that 18th hole, Vee.

257
00:22:59,035 --> 00:23:02,776
What is your heart
telling you to do right now?

258
00:23:03,810 --> 00:23:05,397
And who are you doing it for?

259
00:24:11,959 --> 00:24:13,276
Unbelievable!

260
00:24:13,301 --> 00:24:15,774
Pro Vee turns it around
on the final hole,

261
00:24:15,799 --> 00:24:18,928
edging out Pro Jin
by just one stroke!

262
00:24:18,953 --> 00:24:20,867
Amazing! Amazing!

263
00:24:20,892 --> 00:24:23,454
Pro Vee did it! She did it!

264
00:24:23,479 --> 00:24:27,475
With a score of -13,
while Pro Jin finishes at -12,

265
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:29,748
losing by the narrowest
of margins!

266
00:24:44,378 --> 00:24:45,696
Oh, my God!

267
00:24:45,735 --> 00:24:46,693
That was so intense!

268
00:24:46,718 --> 00:24:48,697
They were neck and neck
all 18 holes.

269
00:24:48,729 --> 00:24:49,910
It was so close.

270
00:24:49,935 --> 00:24:51,987
- Yeah.
- She even had the advantage.

271
00:24:52,012 --> 00:24:55,795
I can't stop smiling.
She's amazing. Oh, my God!

272
00:25:02,330 --> 00:25:03,568
You were amazing.

273
00:25:12,736 --> 00:25:14,169
Congratulations, my friend.

274
00:25:17,259 --> 00:25:20,261
Thank you.
You played really well today.

275
00:25:21,325 --> 00:25:24,273
But I guess
it wasn't enough to beat you.

276
00:25:25,746 --> 00:25:28,150
And about
what happened that day...

277
00:25:29,280 --> 00:25:30,954
I don't think we need
to talk about it anymore.

278
00:25:31,786 --> 00:25:36,159
Because today made it clear
who the winner is.

279
00:25:36,878 --> 00:25:39,497
As for the past,
let it stay there.

280
00:25:40,155 --> 00:25:41,856
I'm not going
to carry it anymore.

281
00:25:42,539 --> 00:25:45,527
And as for our friendship...

282
00:25:46,626 --> 00:25:49,141
The friendship
that ended that day...

283
00:25:49,879 --> 00:25:51,233
I guess we'll just have to
give it time.

284
00:25:52,542 --> 00:25:55,852
But I believe...
it'll find its way back to us.

285
00:25:58,042 --> 00:25:59,420
Congratulations, my friend.

286
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:25,957
Congratulations.
You both played beautifully.

287
00:26:27,579 --> 00:26:30,748
Losing today doesn't mean
you'll lose forever.

288
00:26:35,071 --> 00:26:36,993
Winning today
wasn't easy either, was it?

289
00:26:41,906 --> 00:26:46,145
Congratulations to Goodview
on becoming an Asian Tour venue.

290
00:26:46,938 --> 00:26:48,020
Thank you.

291
00:26:48,666 --> 00:26:52,414
Facing a stronger opponent
only pushes us to get better.

292
00:26:53,798 --> 00:26:59,626
I hope The Royal Green can be
a worthy rival to Goodview.

293
00:27:00,983 --> 00:27:03,941
I admire what a strong woman
you are, Auntie.

294
00:27:06,450 --> 00:27:08,352
You're a strong young woman, too.

295
00:27:09,701 --> 00:27:13,239
It'd be a shame if we're only
good enough to beat each other.

296
00:27:13,548 --> 00:27:16,248
When we could be good enough
to leave everyone else behind.

297
00:27:16,451 --> 00:27:18,379
There's one thing I believe.

298
00:27:18,404 --> 00:27:20,588
Strong women
don't have to compete

299
00:27:20,613 --> 00:27:22,347
by making another woman fall.

300
00:27:22,465 --> 00:27:25,711
You just have to keep pushing
yourself to climb higher,

301
00:27:25,736 --> 00:27:28,669
without stepping on
or hurting other women.

302
00:27:29,646 --> 00:27:33,060
If you use the strength you have
to create something new,

303
00:27:33,089 --> 00:27:37,278
It could be so much more than
wondering who's better.

304
00:27:39,558 --> 00:27:43,438
Besides, the way we choose to win

305
00:27:43,463 --> 00:27:45,083
says a lot about who we are.

306
00:27:45,993 --> 00:27:49,617
Even if we win,
if we do it dirty,

307
00:27:50,205 --> 00:27:52,408
that's how people
will remember us.

308
00:27:54,059 --> 00:27:56,308
Raising yourself up is harder,

309
00:27:56,806 --> 00:28:00,031
but it's more fulfilling than
tearing someone else down.

310
00:28:01,078 --> 00:28:02,405
That's what I believe.

311
00:28:09,342 --> 00:28:11,837
And with that, the competition
has officially come to an end.

312
00:28:11,862 --> 00:28:13,458
And we have our results.

313
00:28:13,483 --> 00:28:14,935
And now,

314
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:18,318
please welcome Pro Venus to
the stage to receive her trophy

315
00:28:18,343 --> 00:28:23,409
for the All Star Women's
Golf Championship.

316
00:28:26,362 --> 00:28:28,163
And now, we invite
a representative

317
00:28:28,188 --> 00:28:29,647
from Goodview Golf Club

318
00:28:29,671 --> 00:28:33,087
to receive the certificate
granting them hosting rights

319
00:28:33,112 --> 00:28:35,350
for the Asian Tour
later this year.

320
00:28:35,375 --> 00:28:37,375
Oh, my God!

321
00:28:55,755 --> 00:28:57,414
I don't blame you for this.

322
00:29:00,258 --> 00:29:01,773
I blame myself

323
00:29:02,388 --> 00:29:04,896
for trusting a rookie cheater
like you.

324
00:29:05,636 --> 00:29:06,675
Pathetic.

325
00:29:21,532 --> 00:29:24,386
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

326
00:29:24,411 --> 00:29:27,412
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

327
00:29:27,437 --> 00:29:31,170
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

328
00:29:31,195 --> 00:29:33,088
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

329
00:29:33,113 --> 00:29:35,992
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

330
00:29:36,017 --> 00:29:39,454
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

331
00:29:39,479 --> 00:29:44,190
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

332
00:29:44,215 --> 00:29:45,829
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

333
00:29:45,854 --> 00:29:48,752
♪ Say it, say it.
Say "You love me." ♪

334
00:29:48,777 --> 00:29:51,763
♪ Call me, call me.
Call me "Baby." ♪

335
00:29:56,386 --> 00:29:59,335
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

336
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:02,678
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

337
00:30:02,703 --> 00:30:07,389
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

338
00:30:07,414 --> 00:30:09,385
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

339
00:30:11,803 --> 00:30:16,299
Everyone! Miss Nana is here! Yay!

340
00:30:27,574 --> 00:30:33,445
- Vive la vie! Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie! Vive la vie!

341
00:30:53,484 --> 00:30:55,882
I want to thank everyone so much

342
00:30:55,907 --> 00:30:59,433
for helping bring our course
back to the top of the industry.

343
00:31:01,055 --> 00:31:04,699
I couldn't have done any of this
without all of you.

344
00:31:07,641 --> 00:31:09,380
Thank you
from the bottom of my heart.

345
00:31:14,499 --> 00:31:17,356
And thank you, Pro Vee,

346
00:31:17,381 --> 00:31:19,610
for bringing home the win
for Goodview,

347
00:31:20,094 --> 00:31:22,926
and making us
an Asian Tour venue.

348
00:31:26,603 --> 00:31:28,696
Looks like we've got another
round of hard work ahead of us.

349
00:31:29,698 --> 00:31:32,405
Hmm... What should we do?

350
00:31:32,430 --> 00:31:37,425
Then let me speak for all
the Goodview staff.

351
00:31:39,527 --> 00:31:42,036
We should be thanking you, too,
Miss Nana,

352
00:31:42,559 --> 00:31:45,725
for giving us a reason to get up
and come to work every morning

353
00:31:45,750 --> 00:31:48,766
at Goodview Golf Club.

354
00:31:49,283 --> 00:31:51,955
We're so proud
that we can tell everyone

355
00:31:51,980 --> 00:31:53,980
we work at Goodview.

356
00:31:55,118 --> 00:31:57,135
We love you so much, Miss Nana.

357
00:31:57,175 --> 00:32:00,544
And thank you
for making this place

358
00:32:00,569 --> 00:32:03,000
feel like a second home to us.

359
00:32:03,739 --> 00:32:05,739
Thank you so much, Miss Nana.

360
00:32:06,450 --> 00:32:07,908
We promise, Miss Nana,

361
00:32:07,933 --> 00:32:10,028
we'll give it everything
we've got.

362
00:32:10,068 --> 00:32:11,396
Right, everyone?

363
00:32:11,420 --> 00:32:13,087
- That's right!
- Absolutely!

364
00:32:13,399 --> 00:32:15,257
Vive la vie!

365
00:32:15,282 --> 00:32:19,949
- Vive la vie! Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie! Vive la vie!

366
00:32:19,974 --> 00:32:21,399
Everyone! Everyone!

367
00:32:21,764 --> 00:32:24,430
There's one more
piece of good news

368
00:32:24,455 --> 00:32:26,218
I'd like to share with everyone.

369
00:32:26,242 --> 00:32:29,867
Management has just finalized
our recent financial results.

370
00:32:30,894 --> 00:32:33,205
This month is the first month

371
00:32:33,230 --> 00:32:37,145
our course has turned a profit
in nearly a year.

372
00:32:37,170 --> 00:32:40,092
And this is something
we can all be proud of.

373
00:32:40,117 --> 00:32:41,856
Oh, my God!

374
00:32:41,881 --> 00:32:43,215
Vive la vie!

375
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:48,996
- Vive la vie! Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie! Vive la vie!

376
00:32:49,021 --> 00:32:52,702
- Vive la vie! Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie! Vive la vie!

377
00:32:52,727 --> 00:32:55,005
Oh! Your dad is here, Miss Nana!

378
00:32:56,779 --> 00:32:58,479
You finally did it, dear.

379
00:32:58,504 --> 00:33:00,996
And you did it even faster
than I planned.

380
00:33:01,259 --> 00:33:02,449
You did great, sweetheart.

381
00:33:02,474 --> 00:33:03,928
I'm so proud of you.

382
00:33:05,166 --> 00:33:07,510
So Nana can go back
to France now, right, Dad?

383
00:33:07,535 --> 00:33:10,203
Of course.
A promise is a promise.

384
00:33:10,228 --> 00:33:14,841
Because now, with the plans,
projects, and team you've built,

385
00:33:14,866 --> 00:33:20,746
I'm confident our course will
continue to turn a profit.

386
00:33:20,948 --> 00:33:25,378
And you still have your chemo
treatments under my supervision.

387
00:33:25,403 --> 00:33:27,132
Hmm. All right, son.

388
00:33:30,133 --> 00:33:31,934
I don't have anything
to worry about now.

389
00:33:32,473 --> 00:33:35,937
From now on,
you have my green light.

390
00:33:35,962 --> 00:33:39,154
Whatever you want to do,
give it your all.

391
00:33:41,557 --> 00:33:42,676
Thank you, Dad.

392
00:33:45,693 --> 00:33:46,836
I'm proud of you, sweetheart.

393
00:33:51,735 --> 00:33:53,012
Come on, clap for her!

394
00:33:53,037 --> 00:33:56,139
Why are you all
just standing there smiling?

395
00:33:56,782 --> 00:34:00,192
With profits like these,
maybe we'll get a bonus.

396
00:34:00,217 --> 00:34:02,973
You're all standing around
like we're having a campfire.

397
00:34:03,359 --> 00:34:05,594
- Fantastic!
- Come on!

398
00:34:05,802 --> 00:34:07,802
Thank you, sweetheart.
Thank you, everyone.

399
00:34:24,559 --> 00:34:26,356
Why did you call me, Ms. Yupadee?

400
00:34:27,152 --> 00:34:28,564
If this is
about the competition...

401
00:34:28,589 --> 00:34:29,382
Sit down.

402
00:34:29,706 --> 00:34:33,305
Or would you rather stand?
I won't keep you long.

403
00:34:49,932 --> 00:34:51,819
The fertilizer expenses
from last month.

404
00:34:52,644 --> 00:34:54,024
There are
several duplicate claims

405
00:34:54,049 --> 00:34:55,318
amounting to
hundreds of thousands.

406
00:34:58,169 --> 00:35:01,376
The green maintenance expenses
don't add up either.

407
00:35:02,101 --> 00:35:05,110
And there are equipment expenses

408
00:35:06,237 --> 00:35:08,769
and receiving reports
for goods never ordered.

409
00:35:11,239 --> 00:35:13,635
- It's actually like this...
- I don't want to waste my time

410
00:35:13,660 --> 00:35:15,955
listening to you
make up more stories.

411
00:35:19,202 --> 00:35:20,772
I used to think

412
00:35:21,795 --> 00:35:24,616
you could be
an important player for me,

413
00:35:24,641 --> 00:35:26,491
someone who could be
useful to me.

414
00:35:27,181 --> 00:35:28,355
But I was wrong.

415
00:35:29,346 --> 00:35:31,702
You're terrible
at playing the villain.

416
00:35:33,705 --> 00:35:35,555
And now you're trying
to play games with me?

417
00:35:39,615 --> 00:35:41,251
You miscalculated, kid.

418
00:35:44,801 --> 00:35:47,822
- I can explain. Really.
- Don't bother explaining.

419
00:35:48,659 --> 00:35:52,900
It'll only make you look worse
than you already do.

420
00:35:55,621 --> 00:35:57,109
Let me make one thing clear.

421
00:35:57,638 --> 00:36:00,877
I'm not as kind as
that Nana girl.

422
00:36:00,902 --> 00:36:02,472
I'm not letting this slide.

423
00:36:09,510 --> 00:36:12,729
You'll remain an employee here
for one more day.

424
00:36:13,821 --> 00:36:16,511
To settle
everything you've stolen.

425
00:36:17,757 --> 00:36:21,570
And I expect every last penny

426
00:36:21,595 --> 00:36:24,463
to be in my account by tomorrow.

427
00:36:25,835 --> 00:36:27,023
Otherwise...

428
00:36:29,136 --> 00:36:30,350
I'll press charges.

429
00:36:31,098 --> 00:36:32,434
Can I have seven days?

430
00:36:34,785 --> 00:36:36,904
I said tomorrow.
That means tomorrow.

431
00:36:40,007 --> 00:36:41,031
Oh.

432
00:36:44,491 --> 00:36:45,970
I almost forgot one thing.

433
00:36:47,098 --> 00:36:48,745
Consider this a personal request.

434
00:36:51,172 --> 00:36:54,107
Don't tell anyone
you ever worked here.

435
00:36:55,139 --> 00:36:56,202
I'm embarrassed.

436
00:37:31,066 --> 00:37:32,094
I lost.

437
00:37:33,782 --> 00:37:34,792
Yes.

438
00:37:35,610 --> 00:37:36,817
You lost.

439
00:37:37,586 --> 00:37:39,988
A loss is just a loss.

440
00:37:40,980 --> 00:37:42,061
It's just a loss, right?

441
00:37:43,459 --> 00:37:46,170
But you got something
out of it, too.

442
00:37:47,610 --> 00:37:48,649
What's that?

443
00:37:49,206 --> 00:37:52,176
You got to let go
of what was weighing on you.

444
00:37:53,058 --> 00:37:55,073
You got your friend Pro Vee back.

445
00:37:55,567 --> 00:37:58,184
And now you have me
by your side, too.

446
00:37:59,901 --> 00:38:00,972
Thank you.

447
00:38:02,166 --> 00:38:03,403
For what?

448
00:38:06,658 --> 00:38:09,210
I've decided
to leave The Royal Green.

449
00:38:10,571 --> 00:38:11,745
Why?

450
00:38:12,450 --> 00:38:14,026
It's not my place anymore.

451
00:38:15,758 --> 00:38:18,560
Then...
why not come back to Goodview?

452
00:38:20,634 --> 00:38:21,867
I don't think so.

453
00:38:25,938 --> 00:38:27,579
I have a bigger dream.

454
00:38:27,683 --> 00:38:28,763
What dream?

455
00:38:28,962 --> 00:38:31,192
Competing internationally
on the LPGA Tour.

456
00:38:31,816 --> 00:38:33,054
You're aiming that high?

457
00:38:33,649 --> 00:38:35,079
I want to go all the way.

458
00:38:35,806 --> 00:38:39,392
Then you'll need
a good manager, won't you?

459
00:38:39,417 --> 00:38:42,865
From what I know,
there's training to plan,

460
00:38:42,890 --> 00:38:45,670
tournaments to enter,

461
00:38:45,940 --> 00:38:49,252
sponsors to find, not to mention
travel arrangements.

462
00:38:49,277 --> 00:38:52,367
- And then there's...
- Interested in the job?

463
00:38:53,535 --> 00:38:55,148
Can I fill out an application?

464
00:38:55,911 --> 00:38:58,507
No need. Let's just go straight
to the interview.

465
00:39:04,399 --> 00:39:06,041
Is this your way
of getting back at me?

466
00:39:07,932 --> 00:39:09,146
Hmm...

467
00:39:10,130 --> 00:39:13,175
Start at 100
and keep subtracting 7.

468
00:39:15,023 --> 00:39:21,618
93, 86, 79, 72, 65.

469
00:39:21,643 --> 00:39:22,669
That's enough.

470
00:39:22,694 --> 00:39:24,257
Next, I'll ask you
rapid-fire questions.

471
00:39:24,282 --> 00:39:25,092
Go ahead.

472
00:39:25,116 --> 00:39:26,323
- One or two?
- One.

473
00:39:26,348 --> 00:39:28,312
- Bedroom or bathroom?
- Bathroom.

474
00:39:28,630 --> 00:39:30,930
Living room or in the car?

475
00:39:32,314 --> 00:39:33,758
- Left or right?
- Right.

476
00:39:34,150 --> 00:39:36,230
- Morning or night?
- Night.

477
00:39:37,033 --> 00:39:39,002
- Black or pink?
- Pink.

478
00:39:39,033 --> 00:39:40,256
Will you be my girlfriend?

479
00:39:43,150 --> 00:39:44,191
Excuse me?

480
00:39:44,841 --> 00:39:46,841
Answer me.
Will you be my girlfriend?

481
00:39:50,891 --> 00:39:51,977
Yes.

482
00:39:54,216 --> 00:39:55,549
Are you sure?

483
00:39:56,463 --> 00:39:57,784
Absolutely.

484
00:40:01,073 --> 00:40:03,795
So, does that mean I got the job?

485
00:40:06,515 --> 00:40:09,501
Then I'll ask for
my salary in advance.

486
00:40:19,442 --> 00:40:21,259
A talented manager like you

487
00:40:21,775 --> 00:40:23,775
deserves more than
just an advance.

488
00:40:24,146 --> 00:40:25,910
You deserve a special bonus, too.

489
00:40:27,214 --> 00:40:30,079
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

490
00:40:30,104 --> 00:40:34,305
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

491
00:40:36,188 --> 00:40:39,326
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

492
00:40:39,351 --> 00:40:41,929
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

493
00:40:41,955 --> 00:40:47,577
♪ Sometimes this tender heart
may despair ♪

494
00:40:47,602 --> 00:40:50,784
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

495
00:40:50,809 --> 00:40:53,207
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

496
00:40:53,232 --> 00:40:57,411
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

497
00:40:57,436 --> 00:41:03,600
♪ Even when the storm rolls in
or tears fill your eyes ♪

498
00:41:03,625 --> 00:41:07,642
♪ Turn around, you'll find me
right by your side ♪

499
00:41:07,667 --> 00:41:11,265
♪ Even when the whole world
turns unkind ♪

500
00:41:11,290 --> 00:41:13,595
♪ You won't be left behind ♪

501
00:41:13,620 --> 00:41:18,723
♪ Cause I'll always be right here
by your side ♪

502
00:41:24,844 --> 00:41:25,885
Pro Vee.

503
00:41:28,445 --> 00:41:33,088
Everything at the course
is going really well.

504
00:41:33,998 --> 00:41:36,696
We're starting to turn
a profit again.

505
00:41:36,927 --> 00:41:40,446
All the projects we've worked on
are going according to plan.

506
00:41:41,530 --> 00:41:44,649
Dad's started
his chemo treatments,

507
